.TH TELNET 1 "June 30, 2026"
.SH NAME
telnet \- small TELNET client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B telnet
[
.B \-K
.I key
]
[
.B \-c
.I command
]
.I host
[
.I port
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Telnet
opens an interactive TCP connection and performs the small subset of TELNET
option negotiation needed by the RetroBSD network port.
.PP
The client accepts remote echo and suppress-go-ahead options, rejects other
options, doubles TELNET IAC bytes, and puts the local terminal in raw mode
while connected.
.PP
With
.B \-K ,
the client performs a RetroBSD pre-shared-key handshake before TELNET option
negotiation and encrypts the byte stream.  The peer must be
.IR telnetd (8)
started with the same key.  This is a compact lab transport, not TLS or SSH.
.PP
With
.B \-c ,
the client sends one command line after connecting, closes the write side of
the TCP connection, and continues reading until the server closes the session.
.SH BUGS
Plain TELNET mode is not encrypted.  The
.B \-K
mode avoids plaintext, but it is not compatible with standard TELNET clients
and should not be confused with SSH.
